Rebuild the H.264 PPS with the stream's real default reference counts.

VA-API does not carry num_ref_idx_l{0,1}_default_active_minus1, so the bridge
guessed min(DPB, 3) - 1. When the guess is wrong and the stream uses weighted
prediction (x264 -preset fast), MediaCodec reads pred_weight_table with the
wrong length, drops pictures and vaSyncSurface never returns. Each slice NAL
reaches the driver whole, so read num_ref_idx_active_override_flag from its
header: a P or B slice without an override uses the defaults, and its active
counts from the VA slice parameters are the defaults. The PPS is resent when
they change. Streams where every slice overrides keep the old guess, which
does not matter to them.

Also let the launcher set the SPS max_num_reorder_frames through
TERMUX_VA_H264_REORDER_FRAMES, as 0103 does for HEVC.

